Adjust folder names only if the repo already uses different ones; then follow the existing layout.

## Naming

- Backend packages/modules: lowercase, domain-based (`ticket`, `user`, `auth`)
- Frontend folders/components: match existing frontend conventions once the app exists
- Branches: `cursor/<ticket-or-topic>-<short-summary>` or `feature/<short-summary>`
- Do not commit secrets, `.env` with credentials, or private keys

## Change discipline

- Prefer the smallest change that completes the request
- Do not refactor unrelated code
- Do not add dependencies unless required for the task
- Do not introduce new frameworks or patterns when an existing one fits
- Keep backend and frontend contracts aligned when both change

## Rule ownership

- Java/Spring implementation → `java-springboot` rule
- REST contracts → `api-standards` rule
- Tests → `testing` rule
- Documentation → documentation skill
- Review / spec / test workflows → `.cursor/commands/`

Do not duplicate those instructions here.

## Agent behavior

- Follow existing code style in the touched area
- Ask before large structural changes
- Never hardcode credentials or disable security controls
